From: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] vmess: restore legacy alterId outbound authentication

Carry alterId through JSON, protobuf and memory accounts, restoring the
legacy HMAC-MD5 authentication and AES-CFB request/response headers for
explicitly configured nonzero alterId outbounds. Keep alterId=0 on AEAD
and reject legacy inbound settings, whose server support is not restored.
Initialize response keys before the concurrent request/response tasks.
Use the current timestamp, as Mihomo does, for legacy server compatibility.

Adapt the legacy client handshake from Xray v1.5.5. Cover alternative UUID
vectors, config/protobuf round trips, TCP/UDP payloads, both AEAD payload
ciphers and malformed legacy responses; retain existing AEAD header tests.

Reference: https://github.com/XTLS/Xray-core/blob/v1.5.5/proxy/vmess/encoding/client.go
Signed-off-by: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>

